====Freedom of the City====
* 23 February 1987 – 27 April 2022: [[Freedom of the City#Freedom_of_the_City_of_York|Freedom of the City of York]]<ref name="Sky News-2022">{{cite news|url=https://news.sky.com/story/prince-andrew-york-councillors-unanimously-vote-to-remove-dukes-freedom-of-the-city-12600283|title=Prince Andrew: York councillors unanimously vote to remove Duke's freedom of the city|work=[[Sky News]]|date=27 April 2022|accessdate=27 April 2022|archive-date=17 December 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241217212103/https://news.sky.com/story/prince-andrew-york-councillors-unanimously-vote-to-remove-dukes-freedom-of-the-city-12600283|url-status=live}}</ref>
* 2012: [[Freedom of the City of London]]<ref name=decorations/>
In 2012 Andrew was awarded the [[Freedom of the City of London]] "by virtue of patrimony", his father Prince Philip being a Freeman.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Petrakos |first=Kyriakos |date=2026-03-09 |title=The privileges Andrew can't lose – including herding sheep across London Bridge |url=https://inews.co.uk/news/privileges-andrew-cant-lose-herding-sheep-london-bridge-4278489 |access-date=2026-07-26 |work=The i Paper}}</ref> In May 2026, the City of London Corporation passed a motion to censure Mountbatten-Windsor.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2026-05-26 |title=City of London instructs officers “to pursue steps to lawfully remove” Freedom of the City from Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor |url=https://www.localgovernmentlawyer.co.uk/governance/396-governance-news/100601-city-of-london-instructs-officers-to-pursue-steps-to-lawfully-remove-freedom-of-the-city-from-andrew-mountbatten-windsor |access-date=2026-07-27 |work=Local Government Lawyer}}</ref> In July 2026, the City of London Corporation published a  plan to remove the Freedom of the City.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2026-07-27 |title=Draft legal opinion details plan to remove Freedom of City of London honour from Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor |url=https://www.localgovernmentlawyer.co.uk/governance/396-governance-news/101235-draft-legal-opinion-details-plan-to-remove-freedom-of-city-of-london-honour-from-andrew-mountbatten-windsor |access-date=2026-07-26 |work=Local Government Lawyer}}</ref>

